titre $ Key to British genera
com$Pegler D.N. et al. 1995 British puffballs earthstars and stinkhorns/adapt GF sept 2013

Nota: les clés au format normalisée .CLE sont avantageusement exmploitées par le logiciel 'Mycocle' (gratuit), téléchargeable sur 'http://mycolim.free.fr/DOC_SML/mycoCLE/Charg_Mycocle.htm'

1,2 $ Sterile base (subgleba) abs.ent or rudimentary
1,3 $ Sterile base prominent
1,0$ source : Pegler, D.N.; Laessoe, T.;; Spooner, B. 1995. British puffballs, earthstars and stinkhorns. 

2,0 $ Fruitbody more than 10 cm in diam., sessile; capillitium of Lycoperdon-type $ Calvatia
2,0 $ Fruitbody less than 6 cm diam; capillitium either of Bovista-, of intermediate or of Lycoperdon-type. $ Bovista
3,0 $ Gleba separated from the sterile base by a well developed membrane (diaphragm); capillitium of Lycoperdon-type, non-poroid $ Vascellum
3,4 $ Diaphragm not developed; capillitium of various types, poroid or non-poroid
4,0 $ Fruitbody turbinate with rooting base, and a wide opening; capillitium of Bovista type . $ Bovistella
4,5 $ Not this combination of characters
5,0 $ Fruitbody large with disintegrating endoperidium; capillitium of Lycoperdon-type but with sinuous pores $ Handkea
5,6 $ Fruitbody small to medium, endoperidium not disintegrating; capillitium of various types
6,0 $ Subgleba compact, poroid structure only visible under a lens; opens by slit or rarely by pore; capillitium of various types $ Bovista
6,0 $ Subgleba poroid to naked eye; opens by a distinct pore; capillitium of Lycoperdon-type $ Lycoperdon
